      "side": 1,
      "message": "Grpc_Enable defaults to true and Grpc_Addr to 0.0.0.0, and this credential type covers every service on the server, not only metrics. LocalServerCredentials(LOCAL_TCP) only checks that the peer is on loopback, so any local user who can open 127.0.0.1:50051 can call shutdown, export add/remove, grace, and QoS. Should ssl stay the default, with local opt-in and bound to loopback? Callers in nfsServiceClient.cc still use SslCredentials, so would those still connect?\n\n@ffilzlnx@mindspring.com\nWhat would be a better way?",
      "revId": "ee9ffef9301d699ef26534522e234a37d8bf3a6b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
